      "id": "M4117-B",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "B. A fictional process model defines m(t) as a trailing moving average and r(t)=x(t)-m(t). It encodes r(t) as h, computes u=h+F(h), and concatenates u with the separately encoded m(t) before classification. A separate reporting statistic is e=y-y_hat. The draft calls all four operations \"residual connections\" and claims they remove noise and prove generalization. Review the names in Chinese and provide two or three connected English method sentences using only these facts. Give two checked Chinese sources for any base network-connection translation you recommend, with their passage locations. Do not change the model or invent evaluations.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Distinguish trend remainder, additive residual connection, concatenation and prediction error by operands.",
        "Retain legitimate residual-connection terminology for h+F(h) and use the two Chinese journal records.",
        "Write connected extraction, addition and classification without invented noise-removal/generalization results."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Rename every operation as residual connection or forbid the genuine additive connection.",
        "Treat translation evidence as endorsement of full source architectures or outcomes."
      ],
