    {
      "id": "M4117-C",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "C. An author proposes a newly defined \"Elapsed-Interval Gate\": its input is the time since each sensor measurement, its output is one multiplicative weight per encoded measurement, and it performs no human-age or equipment-aging estimation. One previous paper uses exactly that component name; two other papers define generic feature gates without elapsed-time inputs. The author asks whether the new component name may remain in their manuscript, whether the complete name belongs in a shared glossary of established mechanism families, and whether its Chinese name should be “年龄门控”. Give a Chinese answer and one short English method sentence. No other sources or implementation claims are supplied.",
